Sponsored by Ting Mobile.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:04.863
Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:06.870
It's time to think like
a defamation lawyer.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.500
Legal Eagle has covered
defamation lawsuits many times.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.657
Remember the good old days of

00:01:10.657 --> 00:01:13.240
Devin Nunes versus Devin Nunes' cow,

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.520
Tulsi Gabbard versus Hillary Clinton,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.760
and Donald Trump versus
the New York Times.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.580
Well, all of those cases got dismissed

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.820
because they were just not good claims.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.010
It's really hard to make
a viable defamation claim.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.990
However, when the leader
of the Western world

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.460
makes claims about voting
systems calling them rigged,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.970
he empowers other people
to repeat those claims

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.980
even when they're patently false.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.950
That's why the pro-Trump media
ecosystem is totally awash

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.830
in conspiracy theories involving
dominion and Smartmatic,

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.170
two of the companies which provided

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:42.607
election support in 2020.

00:01:42.607 --> 00:01:44.110
And it was only a matter of time

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.130
before those companies and
their employees fought back.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:48.730
And one lawsuit has been filed,

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.680
several other lawsuits
have been threatened

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.084
and Trump-allied media is retracting

00:01:53.084 --> 00:01:54.900
those claims like crazy.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.610
So let's take a look at
the suits that Dominion

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.680
and Smartmatic have filed
and threatened to file

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.780
against President Trump
and his surrogates.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.730
But before we dig into those
lawsuits, a word of warning.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.760
It's very easy to get
caught up in cheering people

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.970
using the institutions of
government to stifle speech

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.430
that we don't agree with.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.720
But the First Amendment
exists for a reason.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.380
It protects speech that we like

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.880
and speech that we don't like.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.010
And in the past, when
people have filed suit

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.020
against the New York Times,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.173
or when President Trump filed suit

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:23.100
against a tiny TV station in Wisconsin,

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.720
it was clear that these
defamation suits were bogus

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.120
because those plaintiffs
would never be able

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.953
to meet their burden.

00:02:28.953 --> 00:02:30.702
It's hard to make a defamation claim

00:02:30.702 --> 00:02:32.300
and for very good reason.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.380
But just because we think that
what's being stated is false,

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.407
or we might think that the
people who are propagating

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:41.870
these falsities are, let's
say misinformed at best,

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.810
that doesn't mean it
should be any less hard

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.210
for someone to be able to prove

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.730
a defamation claim against them.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:47.760
It's my personal opinion,

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.900
but I think that the First
Amendment is quite a good thing

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.890
in our society

00:02:51.890 --> 00:02:54.559
and we should be very, very
reluctant to cheer on anyone

00:02:54.559 --> 00:02:58.310
making a claim that could
end up stifling speech

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.790
that we just don't agree with.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.410
And additionally, in another context

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.420
or even in this particular context,

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:06.120
this is a corporation
trying to stifle criticism

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.630
against that corporation.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:10.200
It just so happens that in
this particular context,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.560
it seems like the criticisms
are all in bad faith

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.410
and are completely made up and false.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.610
But with that warning out of the way,

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.500
let's talk about the
lawsuits that have been filed

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.470
with regards to the Dominion
and Smartmatic voting machines.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.290
The first lawsuit that was
filed was by an employee

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:25.400
of Dominion, which is a company
that makes voting machines.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.430
In 2020, Dominion partnered

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.930
with more than 1,300
jurisdictions in the United States

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.160
to provide various
elections support services.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.568
The plaintiff is Eric
Coomer, he's the director

00:03:34.568 --> 00:03:37.800
of product strategy and
security for Dominion.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.410
And if you haven't heard of Dr. Coomer,

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.240
it's probably because you
weren't spending enough time

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.910
consuming pro-Trump
media like Newsmax, OANN

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.860
and your uncle's Facebook page.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.230
Because there he's
practically a celebrity.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:50.110
In the aftermath of Biden's victory,

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.970
conspiracy theories about Dr.
Coomer spread like wildfire

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.280
all over conservative media.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.041
This started with a story
told by an "entrepreneur"

00:03:57.041 --> 00:03:59.860
and podcast host Joseph Oltman,

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.706
who claims he eavesdropped
on an Antifa conference call

00:04:03.706 --> 00:04:06.650
where Antifa activists
discussed their evil plans.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:08.470
During this conference call, Oltman says

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.530
that someone who introduced
himself as Eric from Dominion

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.340
stated he would ensure the
election went to Joe Biden.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.200
Here's Oltman telling Eric Metaxas

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.710
that he infiltrated Antifa.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:22.120
- I had a group of people,
and we infiltrated Antifa.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:23.230
- Then Oltman discovered

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:26.410
that there was a Dominion
employee on the line, allegedly.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.130
- You know, this guy
named Eric started talking

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.930
and then somebody asked who Eric was.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:34.140
And they said, "Eric's a Dominion guy."

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.410
- Then Eric from Dominion
said he was going to just,

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.380
you know, rig the entire election.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.830
- And I'm paraphrasing this, right?

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.845
So I didn't write down
word for word what he said,

00:04:41.845 --> 00:04:44.610
but Eric responds, "Don't
worry about the election.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.570
Trump's not gonna win.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.782
I've made effing sure of that."

00:04:47.782 --> 00:04:50.147
- He made effing sure of that.

00:04:50.147 --> 00:04:52.520
Effing means very, very.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.090
- Oltman offered no explanation

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.780
of how he allegedly infiltrated the call,

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.210
nor does he have a recording of it.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.780
Nevertheless, Oltman decided

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.050
that the Eric was actually Eric Coomer.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.690
He then decided that this was proof

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.270
that Dr. Coomer may have
just rigged the election

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.103
for Joe Biden.

00:05:06.103 --> 00:05:07.147
And within days, the hashtags,

00:05:07.147 --> 00:05:09.330
#EricCoomer, #ExposeEricCoomer

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.980
and #ArrestEricCoomer were
trending on social media.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:13.660
And of course, President Trump published

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:15.090
similar false statements on Twitter,

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:17.610
alleging that Dominion had
interfered with the election.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.410
Eric Trump tweeted a photo of Dr. Coomer

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.030
and alleged that he rigged the election.

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.320
The other defendants published
Oltman's false allegations

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.180
about Dr. Coomer and Oltman appeared

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.830
on YouTube videos, radio
programs, and television shows.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:30.130
The hosts of these programs
repeated the false allegations.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.570
And for example, Michelle
Malkin interviewed Oltman

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:35.270
and started tweeting his
allegations as if they were true.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.890
Quote, Trump's campaign
lawyers identified Dr. Coomer

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.389
in a nationally televised press conference

00:05:39.389 --> 00:05:40.481
where they described him as

00:05:40.481 --> 00:05:44.860
"a vicious, vicious man",
who is "close to Antifa".

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.677
And falsely claimed that Dr. Coomer,

00:05:46.677 --> 00:05:49.680
"specifically says that they're
going to fix this election"

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.690
and that he "had the election
rigged for Mr. Biden".

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:54.870
So seemingly in response
to these allegations,

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.050
Dr. Coomer sued all of the
defendants for defamation

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.220
and intentional infliction
of emotional distress.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:00.571
He also sued them for civil conspiracy,

00:06:00.571 --> 00:06:02.420
alleging they coordinated with each other

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.850
to spread lies about Dr. Coomer himself.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:08.350
Okay, so those are the facts
as alleged in the lawsuit.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.880
But before we dig into
this particular lawsuit,

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.070
let's examine what you have to prove

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.470
to actually make a claim for defamation.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.610
Now, as you probably know,

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:19.450
defamation is making a provably
false statement of fact

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.000
about a person or a company.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.700
Yes, companies can be
the victim of defamation.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.650
But what are the elements?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.030
What do you have to prove to make

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:27.650
a defamation claim in court?

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.700
Well, first, the content
of the communication

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.500
has to be factual in nature.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.810
An opinion is not defamation.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.450
So if you get on Yelp
and write a savage review

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.530
of Popeye's chicken
sandwich, this is an opinion.

00:06:39.530 --> 00:06:40.840
It's not fact.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.190
The internet may ratio you

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:44.270
for preferring the Chick-fil-A sandwich,

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.370
but Popeye's can't sue you
for failing to recognize

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:47.940
the factual truth because there is

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.330
no factual truth to recognize,

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:52.990
most opinion is protected under
First Amendment free speech.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.190
But on the other hand, if
you write a bad review,

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.930
because you say that your chicken sandwich

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.940
had a human finger in it,

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.520
well that's not an opinion anymore.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.670
That's a verifiable provable fact.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:04.268
And if that's false, it could give rise

00:07:04.268 --> 00:07:06.080
to a claim for defamation.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.560
Which takes us to the second element,

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.470
the content of the
communication must be false.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:13.100
Someone can say something
mean that might cause harm

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.410
to another person's reputation.

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.760
Just because you've harmed
someone's reputation

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.020
doesn't mean that you
have committed defamation,

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.860
but that reputation harming
statement must in fact be true.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.520
If it is true, it doesn't
constitute defamation.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.950
If it's false and you have
impugned someone's character,

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:29.440
it's possible that that might give rise

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.360
to a defamation claim.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.510
That's why we say the truth

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.470
is an absolute defense to defamation.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:34.900
It does get a little bit wonky

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.020
because truth is both
an affirmative defense,

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.980
something the defense can prove to defeat

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:40.180
a claim of defamation,

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:43.010
but it's also an element that
the plaintiff has to prove.

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:45.300
They have to prove that
the original communication

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.650
was in fact false.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.560
But that takes us to the third element

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.010
which is that the content is made

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.800
with either negligence or actual malice.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:55.010
When a private person
brings a defamation claim,

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:56.960
they need to only show
negligence by the party

00:07:56.960 --> 00:07:58.900
who published the
communication or statement.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.190
In other words, that
the person was negligent

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:04.520
in saying something
that was in fact false.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.320
But you probably know that public figures

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:08.770
must prove an allegedly
defamatory statement

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:10.770
was made with what's called actual malice.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.420
Now actual malice has absolutely nothing

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:14.430
to do with maliciousness.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.050
If you take anything away from this video,

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:18.573
it is that actual malice is
not about the maliciousness

00:08:18.573 --> 00:08:21.360
with which someone repeats
something that's false.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.210
Actual malice is just a legal term of art.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:25.900
That means that the person
making the statement

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.390
must have known that
the statement was false,

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:30.194
or that the person making the statement

00:08:30.194 --> 00:08:32.930
made it with reckless
disregard for that truth.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.660
In other words, that's
a pretty high burden

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.970
to show that somewhere was
either knowingly saying something

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.800
that was false or
recklessly saying something

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:40.633
that was false.

00:08:40.633 --> 00:08:43.500
Thus, if you are a public
figure or a celebrity,

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.253
a politician, and often
a private business,

00:08:46.253 --> 00:08:49.030
you're subjected to prove
in your defamation claim

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:52.350
by this higher standard of
proof called actual malice.

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:53.510
Which takes us to the fourth element,

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.130
which is that the content
could be defamation per se.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.410
This is also something that
is often misunderstood.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.255
In most states, there is
a subset of communications

00:09:02.255 --> 00:09:05.430
that are considered so
harmful that damages

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.890
to an injured person's
reputation are assumed,

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.830
and the plaintiff doesn't
need to prove damages.

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:11.776
Generally, if you make
a claim for defamation,

00:09:11.776 --> 00:09:13.890
you have to prove damages.

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:18.770
But for old, old reasons in
law, there are some categories

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:21.610
that are just assumed that a
person's reputation is damaged

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:22.443
if you say it.

00:09:22.443 --> 00:09:23.890
So for example, in New York,

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.340
there are four categories of speech

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.130
where it's defamation per se.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.370
Statements that accuse someone

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:29.940
of committing a serious crime,

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:32.382
statements that injure a
person's business or profession,

00:09:32.382 --> 00:09:35.267
statements that someone
has a loathsome disease,

00:09:35.267 --> 00:09:38.780
and a statement that a person is unchaste.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:43.220
Yes, really, unchastity is
one of the kinds of things

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:44.610
that are defamation per se.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.214
If you are accused of being unchaste,

00:09:46.214 --> 00:09:48.372
you don't have to actually
prove your damages

00:09:48.372 --> 00:09:51.810
in order to make an actual
claim for defamation.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.030
And regarding damages,

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.830
there's generally three different kinds.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.070
This goes for just about
any civil claim you can make

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.030
but it's relevant when
it comes to damages.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:00.990
First, there's special damages.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.430
Those are generally economic,

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:04.950
things that the plaintiff
actually has suffered.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.210
So in the context of defamation,

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.450
that can mean loss of income.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:10.960
It could mean actual loss of business

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:12.530
as a result of the defamation.

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:13.860
And then there's general damages.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:15.180
These are things that are harder to put

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.960
an actual monetary price tag on.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:19.760
Things like emotional
damages, pain, and suffering

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.150
or loss of consortium.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:22.410
Ask your parents about that one.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.750
And then there's punitive damages,

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.390
things that aren't really related

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:27.010
to the injury suffered itself

00:10:27.010 --> 00:10:29.237
but are meant to actually
punish the defendant.

00:10:29.237 --> 00:10:31.120
Things that are meant to prevent them

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:32.217
from doing things again.

00:10:32.217 --> 00:10:34.450
And then finally, let's talk
about some of the defenses

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.440
that you can raise to
a claim of defamation.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.830
Obviously, you can show that the statement

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.330
that you made was true,
or substantially true

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.530
and that will generally
defeat a claim for defamation.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.690
You can also show that
the statement at issue

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.313
is one of opinion,
rather than one of fact.

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:48.380
So with that background,

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.500
let's analyze some of the claims here.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:54.160
Defamation is a highly
fact-specific claim to make

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.490
but here we can probably
make some generalizations.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.220
First of all, the claim
communications here

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.420
seem to be factual in nature.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.000
They accuse Mr. Coomer

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.010
of actually doctoring voting machines.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.450
That doesn't seem like an issue

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:08.590
of opinion or of hyperbole.

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:10.374
That seems like a
verifiable fact that could

00:11:10.374 --> 00:11:12.270
or could not be true.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.180
It seems like it's false.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.660
While it's highly
contentious on social media,

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:20.000
the reality seems to be that
these election-related claims

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.280
are almost all made up.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.980
And with respect to the
infiltrated Antifa phone call,

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:27.070
that seems to be pure imagination.

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:28.580
Sometimes you can raise the defense

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.200
that the communications don't actually

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.850
involve the person
claiming the defamation,

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.840
but here the social media posts

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:39.320
and the actual news reports
mention Dr. Coomer by name here.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.880
So it seems like these communications

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.290
are about him specifically.

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:45.340
And of course, until these news reports

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.670
and social media posts ran,

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:49.080
Dr. Coomer was not a household name

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:50.850
and it would be very difficult to prove

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:52.150
that he was a public figure.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.060
And thus, he may benefit
from the lower standard,

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.870
not the actual malice standard

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.150
but simply the negligence
standard, because he could prove

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:02.940
that he is a private person
rather than a public figure.

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.850
So the Eric Coomer defamation lawsuit

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.780
is the main one that's been filed so far,

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.800
but it looks like others
are on the horizon

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.880
from both Dominion and Smartmatic.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.550
Now, Smartmatic and Dominion
have started filing suit

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:15.290
but it doesn't look like
they've sued everyone

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:17.084
that they've threatened, yet.

00:12:17.084 --> 00:12:18.840
But it's probably only a matter of time

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.440
until all of these clowns
receive a summons eventually.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.030
And part of the reason that
they might not have filed so far

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.530
is that many states have laws

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:28.110
requiring a plaintiff to
first request a retraction

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.032
before they can recover
certain types of damages

00:12:30.032 --> 00:12:31.950
in a defamation lawsuit.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.020
And both Dominion and Smartmatic

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.670
are basically scorching the earth

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:37.100
with their cease and desist letters,

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.600
and making certain news
organizations bend over backwards

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:42.980
to try and limit the damages
that they might suffer

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:44.850
in terms of a defamation lawsuit.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.930
And generally, if you
want to know how strong

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.076
your defamation claim is,

00:12:48.076 --> 00:12:49.816
you can tell based on how quickly

00:12:49.816 --> 00:12:51.950
the potential defendants roll over

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.190
and give you a retraction.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:55.370
And it's these kinds of
demands for retractions

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.970
that can lead to hilarious results

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:59.530
like even Newsmax muzzling Mike Lindell,

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:01.400
and an anchor walking away from him

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:02.920
after he started talking about some

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.040
of these unverified accusations.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:08.430
- Can I ask our producers,
can we get out of here please?

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.990
- You know that when even
Newsmax is afraid to touch you,

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.720
number one, you're a complete whack job.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.940
And number two, the retraction
letter is doing its work.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.620
And retraction law is a
really interesting wrinkle

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:21.270
in the sort of defamation lawsuit area.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:23.120
Generally states that have retraction laws

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:25.610
require a plaintiff to
request a retraction

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:26.810
or notify the defendant

00:13:26.810 --> 00:13:29.250
of the allegedly defamatory statement

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.060
before they can file a lawsuit.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:32.910
The request or notice must be made

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.510
within a reasonable period of time

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:37.040
after publication of the
allegedly defamatory statement.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.920
And if the defendant
responds by airing a frank

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.250
and full retraction of
the defamatory statement,

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.520
the defendant will be entitled

00:13:43.520 --> 00:13:46.310
to a reduction in
certain types of damages.

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:48.700
In a majority of states, a
retraction prevents a plaintiff

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.330
from recovering punitive damages

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.840
unless a plaintiff can prove malice.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.440
In those states, even if
the plaintiff proves malice,

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:57.340
a timely retraction can mitigate

00:13:57.340 --> 00:13:59.360
most of the punitive damages.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.450
And some states put the
onus on the plaintiff

00:14:01.450 --> 00:14:03.240
to be able to recover certain damages.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.810
And some states put the
onus on the defendants

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:08.230
to be able to limit their damages.

00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:11.190
So for example, in California,
you have to send a letter

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.500
or else you'll only get economic damages.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.550
But in New York, if the defendant prints

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:16.960
or airs the retraction,

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.750
then the defendant can limit the damages

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.480
to economic damages only.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.760
So a retraction doesn't
end the plaintiff's lawsuit

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.420
but it just reduces the amount

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.810
and type of damages that are
available to the plaintiff.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:29.730
So here Dominion and
Smartmatic have sent letters

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.810
to several people and organizations
which made false claims

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.310
about the 2020 election.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.160
Smartmatic and Dominion have demanded

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:39.020
that the media organizations
retract their false claims.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.210
So let's look at some of
these retraction letters.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:44.290
The first is the Smartmatic
vs Fox and Newsmax.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:46.850
Smartmatic's letter to Fox
News accused the network

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.930
of repeatedly airing false
and defamatory statements

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:49.840
about the company.

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:52.697
Smartmatic said in the letter
that Fox news had aided,

00:14:52.697 --> 00:14:54.770
"a concerted disinformation campaign"

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:57.190
presenting unsupported claims
that the company conspired

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.690
to change the results of the
vote to benefit Joe Biden.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:01.600
Although most of the
statements were made originally

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.300
by Rudy Giuliani and Sidney Powell,

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:06.080
the allegations were repeated
by Fox hosts like Lou Dobbs,

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.040
Jeanine Pirro, and Maria Bartiromo.

00:15:08.040 --> 00:15:10.930
The funny thing is, Smartmatic
did not provide any services

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:12.910
to swing States, nor did it tabulate votes

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:14.250
outside of Los Angeles.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.910
But Fox News said Smartmatic
was literally designed

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:18.140
to change votes without detection

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:21.320
and then send them out of
the country for tabulation.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:23.490
And Newsmax and OANN had pushed

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:26.560
the voting company conspiracies
even harder than Fox News.

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:27.430
- We should make up stories

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:28.450
because that'd be far more interesting.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:31.470
- Fellas, are you sure
all of this is e-ethical?

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:33.780
- Newsmax claim that
Smartmatic had relationships

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.970
with all of the right-wing
scariest monsters;

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:37.073
the Clintons, the Pelosi family,

00:15:37.073 --> 00:15:39.740
George Soros, and Hugo Chavez.

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:41.300
Yet after they received the legal letter,

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.250
they aired a detailed retraction.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.260
Here's a Newsmax host reading
the script like a hostage.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.651
- Newsmax has no evidence to the contrary.

00:15:48.651 --> 00:15:51.830
Dominion has stated the
company has no ownership,

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.775
relationship with the Pelosi family,

00:15:53.775 --> 00:15:57.000
the Feinstein family, the Clinton family,

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.740
Hugo Chavez, or the
government of Venezuela.

00:15:59.740 --> 00:16:02.260
- Newsmax also posted an
article on the website.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:04.280
You can check out the scope
of the admissions here.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.961
So these retractions may
in fact reduce the damages

00:16:06.961 --> 00:16:09.710
that the news organizations face.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:12.210
Though a court does require
that a retraction be made

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:15.410
in the same manner as the
original defamatory statement.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.160
So it's not clear that it's getting quite

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.300
the same sort of coverage

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.080
that the original allegations received,

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.470
which was basically
nonstop on these channels

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.900
for days if not weeks.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:25.556
Of course, if the news organizations

00:16:25.556 --> 00:16:27.880
repeat the false allegations,

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.950
it might undo the retraction
and a claim for defamation

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.210
might have no limits
in terms of the damages

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:34.043
that they can seek.

00:16:34.043 --> 00:16:35.850
And now let's turn to the potential case

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:38.710
of Smartmatic and Dominion versus OANN,

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:42.718
because the OAN Network has its
own interesting relationship

00:16:42.718 --> 00:16:44.700
with defamation claims.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:45.810
- We should make up a bunch of reports

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.421
about how dangerous it is to be alive.

00:16:47.421 --> 00:16:48.380
- Oh boy!

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:50.670
- For one, YouTube
suspended the OAN Network

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.200
for posting false
information about COVID-19.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.420
But on top of that, OAN knows its way

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:56.660
around defamation suit.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:57.990
At least it knows what it's like to be

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.300
on the losing side of a defamation claim.

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:03.360
OAN actually sued Rachel
Maddow last year for defamation

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:04.730
claiming that she called the network,

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:06.420
paid Russian propaganda,

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.380
which I guess Maddow actually did.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.530
Apparently an OAN
contributor was moonlighting

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:13.210
as a writer for Sputnik,
the Kremlin's newspaper.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.210
The lawsuit was dismissed

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:16.350
because the statement
was Maddow's opinion.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:18.840
But here predictably, OAN has doubled down

00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:20.710
on its groundless election fraud claims.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:23.350
The company responded to the
Smartmatic and Dominion letters

00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:27.070
which demanded the OAN
preserve all documents related

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:28.930
to the defamatory statements

00:17:28.930 --> 00:17:30.510
or potentially defamatory statements,

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:33.140
which is a pretty standard
litigation tactic.

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:35.690
By demanding that Smartmatic
and Dominion preserve

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:39.810
all documents related to George
Soros, which is interesting.

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:42.290
And some including the New
York Times have speculated

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.939
that if this defamation
suit were successful,

00:17:44.939 --> 00:17:47.967
it might be enough to shut down OAN.

00:17:47.967 --> 00:17:49.450
And then there's the potential case

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:51.560
of Dominion versus Sidney Powell.

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:54.890
In some, Sidney Powell talked
about Dominion's connections

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:57.500
or purported connections
with Nicolas Maduro,

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.330
the company's use of
algorithms to flip votes,

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:01.520
the founder saying his machines can change

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:02.830
a million votes for Biden,

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.070
its relationship with Smartmatic,

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.480
its relationship with George Soros,

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:06.784
its relationship with Hugo Chavez,

00:18:06.784 --> 00:18:09.304
kickbacks it paid to the state of Georgia,

00:18:09.304 --> 00:18:13.798
its interference in the Hillary
Clinton 2016 primary win,

00:18:13.798 --> 00:18:15.510
and training election workers

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:17.600
all over the country to flip for Biden.

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:20.361
All of these allegations
are demonstrably false

00:18:20.361 --> 00:18:23.640
says Dominion and most rational people.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:26.920
And Powell has stated
them as if they were true.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.770
She wrote about all these
things in blog posts,

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:30.770
went on TV and radio and repeated them,

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:33.170
appeared at rallies and made
false statements in court.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.060
And to further amplify her lies,

00:18:35.060 --> 00:18:36.580
she tagged Donald Trump on Twitter,

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:39.840
ensuring that her claims would
be heard around the world.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:42.430
Now, after sending Sidney
Powell a cease and desist letter

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:45.260
for the ages, Dominion
eventually did file a suit

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:49.370
against her and Dominion
sought $1.3 billion in damages.

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.070
But more on that later.

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.430
Dominion is proceeding
as if it will be treated

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:54.950
as a public figure.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.380
Therefore, the complaint
pleads that Powell acted

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:58.690
with actual malice.

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:00.810
As evidence of malice,
the company accuses her

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:03.390
of lying about every facet
of the vote tallying process.

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:05.940
Dominion claims this is defamation per se

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:08.557
because Powell described
Dominion as the perpetrator of,

00:19:08.557 --> 00:19:10.310
"The greatest crime this century

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.120
if not the life of the world."

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:13.113
Her comments inspired others to say

00:19:13.113 --> 00:19:14.407
that Dominion committed,

00:19:14.407 --> 00:19:16.150
"the greatest crime in the
history of the country."

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:18.930
But as we've talked about,
the difficulty for Dominion

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:21.805
is proving that she
acted with actual malice.

00:19:21.805 --> 00:19:24.522
Because to do so, they
have to prove that she knew

00:19:24.522 --> 00:19:26.560
that what she was doing was wrong

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:29.470
rather than she just was acting
crazy or using hyperbole.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:31.410
And the company's
strategy here is to argue

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.260
that she's in the game for the money.

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:36.490
That's why the emphasis that
she fundraised off the effort,

00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:39.360
that she seems to have a
501(C)(4) group to get the money

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:41.850
and that she ignores all of the evidence

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:44.720
disproving her claims because
(cash register ringing).

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:47.780
As for hyperbole, if Powell
actually confined her comments

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.700
to things like this was the biggest heist

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:50.561
in the history of the world,

00:19:50.561 --> 00:19:52.210
she'd probably have a good argument

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.880
that it was clearly
meant as an exaggeration

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.490
or even opinion.

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:57.996
But Powell's problem here is
that she spouts statistics

00:19:57.996 --> 00:20:00.610
and things that feel like facts,

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.000
and her comments even found their way

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:05.250
into President Trump's phone
call with Brad Raffensperger

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:08.320
which I covered in a
video a few weeks back.

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:10.300
He claimed that the votes were shredded

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:12.443
and flipped and massive
numbers of dead people voted,

00:20:12.443 --> 00:20:15.540
and that Dominion took out
the innards of the machines

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:17.530
and replaced them with, I dunno,

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:18.910
a frozen yogurt machine or something.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:20.850
But Powell makes these same claims

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:23.510
despite the fact that they've
been completely disproven.

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:25.450
And not surprisingly Dominion says

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:28.010
that all of this
naturally severely damaged

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:30.630
the company's reputation,
and undermined its business.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.270
The company would likely have solid proof

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.050
that Powell's claims have
damaged its reputation,

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.590
and almost certainly have correspondence

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:39.674
from existing clients
or prospective clients

00:20:39.674 --> 00:20:42.900
saying that they won't
continue to do business

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:45.880
with Dominion because of all
of these crazy allegations.

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:47.950
Certainly it seems clear that
the fury over these claims

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.560
have created serious pressure
on local elections officials

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.390
to cut ties with Dominion entirely.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:55.300
So for these reasons, dominion
seeks punitive damages

00:20:55.300 --> 00:20:56.940
under both DC and Georgia law

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:58.172
because they claim that the statements

00:20:58.172 --> 00:21:00.730
show willful misconduct,
malice, wantonness,

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.370
and conscious indifference to the facts.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.020
And speaking of legal action,

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:06.949
it's criminal how few people
are actually subscribed

00:21:06.949 --> 00:21:07.860
to this channel.

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:09.220
I was looking through
my analytics and only

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.810
a small percentage of viewers
are actually subscribed.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:13.751
So if you find this video
interesting or informative,

00:21:13.751 --> 00:21:15.390
hit that subscribe button.

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:17.530
And just when you thought
all the fun was over,

00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:19.810
SmartmaticC dropped a complete bomb,

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:22.200
a lawsuit seeking $2.7 billion

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:25.173
against Fox, Fox news, Lou
Dobbs, Maria Bartiromo,

00:21:25.173 --> 00:21:28.400
Jeanine Pirro, Rudy
Giuliani and Sidney Powell.

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:30.290
I covered this very briefly before

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:33.150
but this is a somewhat unusual complaint.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.300
And it's very, very clear

00:21:34.300 --> 00:21:36.000
that the lawyers for Smartmatic know

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.520
that this is as much a PR play
as it is actual litigation.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.050
And the intro to this
particular complaint,

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:45.580
the document that starts the
litigation is pretty epic.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:46.970
It starts with one paragraph.

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.870
The earth is round. Two
plus two equals four.

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.130
Joe Biden Kamala Harris
won the 2020 election

00:21:51.130 --> 00:21:52.920
for president and vice
president of the United States.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:55.240
The election was not
stolen, rigged or fixed.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:57.780
These are facts. They're
demonstrable and irrefutable.

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:59.950
And then the lawsuit goes
into paragraph number two.

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:01.660
Defendants have always known these facts.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:02.950
They knew Joe Biden and Kamala Harris

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:04.480
won the 2020 U.S election.

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:05.940
They knew the election was not stolen.

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:07.900
They knew the election
was not rigged or fixed.

00:22:07.900 --> 00:22:10.520
They knew these truths just as
they knew the earth is round

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:12.160
and two plus two equals four.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:14.660
And then the complaint goes
on in paragraphs 12 and 13.

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:16.750
With this action, Smartmatic says: Enough.

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.530
Facts matter. Truth matters.

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:20.160
Defendants engaged in a conspiracy

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:22.350
to spread disinformation about Smartmatic.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:25.080
They lied and they did so
knowingly and intentionally.

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:27.530
Smartmatic seeks to hold them
accountable for those lies

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:29.890
and for the damage that
their lies have caused.

00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:32.530
Smartmatic brings 16
claims against defendants

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:34.330
for defamation and disparagement.

00:22:34.330 --> 00:22:37.090
Smartmatic seeks to recover
in excess of 2.7 billion

00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:39.840
for the economic and
non-economic damage caused

00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:41.590
by Defendants' disinformation campaign,

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:43.030
as well as punitive damages.

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:44.820
Finally, Smartmatic seeks a declaration

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:46.870
requiring Defendants to
fully and completely retract

00:22:46.870 --> 00:22:48.960
their false statements and implications.

00:22:48.960 --> 00:22:51.850
So a couple of things about
this Smartmatic complaint.

00:22:51.850 --> 00:22:55.010
First is that Dominion filed
a suit for 1.3 billion,

00:22:55.010 --> 00:22:57.740
Smartmatic filed a suit for $2.7 billion

00:22:57.740 --> 00:23:00.400
and those are very, very big numbers.

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:01.880
And if these allegations are true,

00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:04.410
they probably suffered
a great deal of damages.

00:23:04.410 --> 00:23:06.700
But the thing about these
particular complaints,

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:07.980
and any complaint for that matter

00:23:07.980 --> 00:23:10.870
is that these numbers
are completely fanciful.

00:23:10.870 --> 00:23:12.530
You can basically put any number you want

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:13.480
in these complaints.

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:15.780
So just because they put
these billions of dollars

00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:18.840
in damages into the thing that
they're asking for the court,

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:20.460
it has no bearing on the reality.

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.370
It might be true, but most likely,

00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:25.310
it's an inflated number
designed to attract attention.

00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:27.740
And obviously these
numbers attract attention.

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:29.830
And it's impossible not to recognize

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:33.070
that sometimes litigation
is as much about PR

00:23:33.070 --> 00:23:35.410
as it is about actually
getting the damages

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:36.243
that you're owed.

00:23:36.243 --> 00:23:37.450
Now, the second thing is that these suits

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:40.073
are probably stronger than
your average defamation suit.

00:23:40.073 --> 00:23:41.710
In the Smartmatic complaint,

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:44.520
there are over 250 pages of allegations.

00:23:44.520 --> 00:23:46.330
It's clear that these lawyers
have done their homework

00:23:46.330 --> 00:23:47.670
and they're loaded for bear.

00:23:47.670 --> 00:23:49.500
And they talk a lot
about the same statements

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:51.740
and allegations that we've
already covered in this video.

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:54.010
Now in performative defamation suits

00:23:54.010 --> 00:23:56.990
that really don't have
any basis in law or fact,

00:23:56.990 --> 00:23:59.205
like for example, what
Devin Nunes tends to do,

00:23:59.205 --> 00:24:01.830
you get very broad
allegations where the lawyers

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:04.370
characterize the statements,
but don't actually say

00:24:04.370 --> 00:24:07.810
what the statements are
because the claims are BS.

00:24:07.810 --> 00:24:10.840
But here the lawyers
painstakingly put every statement

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:13.820
front and center verbatim
into the complaint,

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:15.450
which lends credence to the idea

00:24:15.450 --> 00:24:17.370
that these lawyers actually believe

00:24:17.370 --> 00:24:19.580
that the statements they're
making accusations about

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:21.390
are potentially defamatory.

00:24:21.390 --> 00:24:23.390
Now, the third thing is
that these complaints

00:24:23.390 --> 00:24:25.690
would probably withstand
a motion to dismiss.

00:24:25.690 --> 00:24:27.090
If you've watched this
channel, you probably know

00:24:27.090 --> 00:24:30.080
that a motion to dismiss is
taking all of the accusations

00:24:30.080 --> 00:24:33.160
the plaintiff alleges as true,
it assumes them to be true.

00:24:33.160 --> 00:24:35.430
It's just testing whether it
would be legally sufficient

00:24:35.430 --> 00:24:36.500
if it was true.

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:38.630
And if you get past the motion to dismiss,

00:24:38.630 --> 00:24:39.880
that means you're into discovery

00:24:39.880 --> 00:24:42.020
where you get to ask
questions and demand documents

00:24:42.020 --> 00:24:42.950
from the other side.

00:24:42.950 --> 00:24:44.810
And when you're in that universe,

00:24:44.810 --> 00:24:46.910
that can be really, really
bad for the defendants

00:24:46.910 --> 00:24:49.110
because broad categories of things

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:50.373
that you don't want disclosed

00:24:50.373 --> 00:24:53.200
probably are disclosable in discovery.

00:24:53.200 --> 00:24:55.150
And then finally, the
fourth thing is that,

00:24:55.150 --> 00:24:57.910
at least in the Smartmatic suit,
there's 16 causes of action

00:24:57.910 --> 00:24:59.630
which normally would give me pause.

00:24:59.630 --> 00:25:02.680
Because you often will just
generate causes of action

00:25:02.680 --> 00:25:06.050
in claims to try and throw
everything against the wall

00:25:06.050 --> 00:25:07.030
and see what sticks.

00:25:07.030 --> 00:25:09.230
But here, all of the causes
of action are for defamation

00:25:09.230 --> 00:25:10.730
or disparagement of false statements,

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:13.491
because they're just talking
about different categories

00:25:13.491 --> 00:25:16.640
of topics of statements that were made.

00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:17.688
So it's not like they're claiming

00:25:17.688 --> 00:25:20.620
16 different laws were broken,

00:25:20.620 --> 00:25:23.330
but rather mainly two
sets of laws were broken.

00:25:23.330 --> 00:25:25.680
It's just, there are different
categories of statements

00:25:25.680 --> 00:25:27.400
that fall into those different buckets.

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:29.155
So the fact that there are 16 claims

00:25:29.155 --> 00:25:31.360
doesn't really give me as much pause

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:33.020
as it would in a different context.

00:25:33.020 --> 00:25:35.260
And then finally Smartmatic
is seeking punitive damages

00:25:35.260 --> 00:25:37.260
amongst other kinds of
damages, which is interesting,

00:25:37.260 --> 00:25:39.550
because punitive damages are hard to get.

00:25:39.550 --> 00:25:41.430
You have to show particularly odious

00:25:41.430 --> 00:25:44.020
and willful conduct to
get punitive damages,

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:46.350
because those damages are
meant to punish the defendant,

00:25:46.350 --> 00:25:47.740
to make sure they don't do it again.

00:25:47.740 --> 00:25:50.670
Regular damages are just
to compensate the victim.

00:25:50.670 --> 00:25:53.800
And if Smartmatic is successful
in proving its claims,

00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:55.670
punitive damages might not be outside

00:25:55.670 --> 00:25:57.170
the realm of possibility.

00:25:57.170 --> 00:25:59.390
This suit is by no means a slam dunk.

00:25:59.390 --> 00:26:01.170
It's probably stronger than average

00:26:01.170 --> 00:26:03.610
when it comes to political
defamation suits.

00:26:03.610 --> 00:26:05.900
But if it were me, I would
not want to be Fox News

00:26:05.900 --> 00:26:07.730
or any of the Fox News
hosts who have been sued

00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:09.030
as a result of these claims.

